guration files directly if access is allowed. Since they\'re facing permission issues, perhaps they need to use a different service account or check the Prometheus server\'s service configuration to see what targets it\'s scraping. If the job name is incorrect, that would explain why the metrics aren\'t showing up. Alternatively, the services might not be exposing metrics properly, or the Prometheus server isn\'t configured to scrape them. The next step would be to verify the scraping targets in Prometheus\'s configuration and ensure that the job name matches what\'s being used in the metrics queries.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get secret -n observe prometheus-k8s-alertmanager-main -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-93134abf1d94b8b1', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 460, 'prompt_tokens': 5403, 'total_tokens': 5863, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdea-cfc2-70a0-b740-bc26ddbd1bdf-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get secret -n observe prometheus-k8s-alertmanager-main -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-93134abf1d94b8b1', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5403, 'output_tokens': 460, 'total_tokens': 5863}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl command:\nError from server (NotFound): secrets "prometheus-k8s-alertmanager-main" not found\n', id='e83789d7-2043-4c29-bde3-73c8498b931e', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-93134abf1d94b8b1'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}