get the config map failed, they should look into secrets or directly check the Prometheus server\'s configuration files. If they can\'t access the config map, they might need to check the Prometheus server\'s logs or configuration files to see what targets are being scraped and if the job name "hotel-reservation" is correctly referenced. \n\nAnother angle is that the metrics endpoint might not be properly exposed by the services. The user should verify if the services in the hotel-reservation namespace are exposing metrics on the correct endpoints (like /metrics) and that Prometheus is configured to scrape those endpoints. If the metrics aren\'t being scraped, the PromQL queries will return empty results, leading to the observed issues.\n\nIn summary, the next step is to check the Prometheus server\'s configuration in the "observe" namespace to ensure it\'s correctly set up to scrape the metrics from the hotel-reservation services. If the config map isn\'t available, they should look into secrets or the server\'s own configuration files to find the scraping targets and job names. This will help determine if the metrics are being collected properly or if there\'s a misconfiguration in the scraping setup.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get all -n observe"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-80e10d7a60e59a4c', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 612, 'prompt_tokens': 5158, 'total_tokens': 5770, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdea-82c2-7bf3-95f2-986a66b6afab-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get all -n observe'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-80e10d7a60e59a4c'