 the service code or logs, the best they can do is infer based on the absence of metrics data and the service endpoints. \n\nTherefore, the answer submitted points out that the services aren't exposing metrics, leading to the monitoring issues. This makes sense as the next step would be to instrument the services with Prometheus to start collecting data.\n</think>\n\nThe root cause of the failure is that the microservices in the hotel-reservation namespace are not exposing metrics via a `/metrics` endpoint. This prevents Prometheus from scraping metrics, resulting in no data being collected. The services likely lack proper instrumentation with Prometheus client libraries, or the metrics endpoints are misconfigured. Without metrics exposure, the application's health and performance cannot be monitored, leading to undetected faults.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 456, 'prompt_tokens': 6946, 'total_tokens': 7402, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdeb-df52-7960-ad95-5a3b5c651b72-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6946, 'output_tokens': 456, 'total_tokens': 7402}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='d491b011-8b2c-409f-9078-6b7eabd92fb1'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to diagnose issues in a hotel reservation application composed of many microservices. They've been using various tools to check the status of services, deployments, metrics, and configurations. \n\nFirst, they started by listing deployments and pods in the hotel-reservation namespace. Everything seemed to be running with READY status, so the initial check didn't show any obvious issues. Then they checked Grafana services and operations, which gave some service names and operations, but not much else.\n\nNext, they tried querying metrics using PromQL. The initial query for http_requests_total didn't return any data, which raised a red flag. They then checked specific operations like /user.User/CheckUser, but again, no metrics. This suggested that the services might not be exposing metrics properly.\n\nThe user then tried to look into Prometheus configurations, checking config maps and service monitors in the 'observe' namespace, but faced permission issues and errors. They also checked endpoints and services in the hotel-reservation namespace, which showed all services were up and reachable. However, the ports listed didn't include a /metrics endpoint, which is crucial for Prometheus scraping.\n\nThe key realization here is that none of the services are exposing metrics. The absence of a /metrics endpoint means Prometheus can't collect data, leading to no metrics being available. This could be due to the services not being instrumented with Prometheus client libraries, or the metrics endpoints not being properly configured. Without these metrics, the system can't monitor performance, detect anomalies, or identify faults.\n\nThe user tried to confirm this by checking the services' ports, but the ports listed (like 8300, 8081, etc.) don't include a standard metrics port (usually 9090 or similar). This indicates that the services aren't set up to expose metrics. Therefore, the root cause is the lack of proper instrumentation and configuration for metrics exposure.\n</think>\n\nThe root cause of the failure is that the microservices in the hotel-reservation namespace are not exposing metrics via a `/metrics` endpoint. This prevents Prometheus from scraping metrics, resulting in no data being collected. The services likely lack proper instrumentation with Prometheus client libraries, or the metrics endpoints are misconfigured. Without metrics exposure, the application's health and performance cannot be monitored, leading to undetected faults.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=488, prompt_tokens=6175, total_tokens=6663, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdeb-f55f-7732-89c0-668793007c7d-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6175, 'output_tokens': 488, 'total_tokens': 6663}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='16294ed5-fde1-47ce-942b-fe9b7170808f')]]
