rrectly set up to discover the targets. The user might need to check the Prometheus logs for any errors related to target scraping. Additionally, ensuring that the metrics endpoints (like /metrics) are accessible and correctly exposed by the services is crucial. \n\nIf the configmap is correctly set up, the next step would be to check the actual metrics endpoints of the services. Using kubectl to exec into a pod and check if the /metrics endpoint is responding could help. If the metrics aren\'t being exposed, the services might need to be configured to include the necessary annotations for Prometheus monitoring. \n\nIn summary, the root cause is likely a misconfiguration in Prometheus setup or the services not exposing metrics properly. The user needs to verify the Prometheus configmap, ensure the job name matches, check the services\' metrics endpoints, and confirm that the metrics are being scraped correctly.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get configmap -n monitoring prometheus-config -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ac172e0fa6c4ec01', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 493, 'prompt_tokens': 4157, 'total_tokens': 4650, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfde9-c479-7d40-ae01-791fc71fdb0b-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get configmap -n monitoring prometheus-config -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ac172e0fa6c4ec01', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4157, 'output_tokens': 493, 'total_tokens': 4650}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl command:\nError from server (NotF