theus client libraries, or the metrics endpoints are misconfigured. Without metrics exposure, the application's health and performance cannot be monitored, leading to undetected faults.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 488, 'prompt_tokens': 6175, 'total_tokens': 6663, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdeb-f55f-7732-89c0-668793007c7d-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6175, 'output_tokens': 488, 'total_tokens': 6663}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='16294ed5-fde1-47ce-942b-fe9b7170808f'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose issues in a hotel reservation application composed of many microservices. They\'ve been using various tools to check the services, deployments, metrics, and configurations. \n\nFirst, they started by listing the deployments in the hotel-reservation namespace. All the deployments were showing as healthy (READY, UP-TO-DATE, AVAILABLE). Then they checked Grafana services and operations, which gave some service names and operations, like the user service\'s /user.User/CheckUser endpoint.\n\nNext, they tried querying Prometheus metrics for http_requests_total with the job "hotel-reservation" and specific operations, but got empty results. This suggested that either the metrics weren\'t being scraped or the job name was incorrect. They checked the Prometheus configuration but faced namespace issues and permission errors, which made it hard to access the correct config maps or secrets.\n\nThen, they checked endpoints in the hotel-reservation namespace and found that ser