trics for the `hotel-reservation` job again, maybe with a broader query to see if any metrics are present. If there are no metrics, that indicates a problem with the service\'s Prometheus exporter configuration. \n\nAlternatively, checking the service\'s logs or using Jaeger traces could help identify if the service is even receiving requests. But since the user has access to metrics tools, focusing on that first makes sense. \n\nAnother angle: maybe the services are using a different namespace or the Prometheus scrape configuration isn\'t set up to monitor that namespace. The user mentioned the namespace is `hotel-reservation`, so the scrape job should include that. \n\nIn any case, the next tool call should be to check the available metrics again, perhaps with a more general query to see if any metrics are being scraped. If there\'s nothing, then the issue is likely with the service\'s metrics setup. If there are metrics, then the specific labels might be different, and the user needs to adjust the query accordingly.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"query": "http_requests_total{job=\\"hotel-reservation\\"}"}', 'name': 'get_metrics'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a1c1ae937d7c271a', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 490, 'prompt_tokens': 3933, 'total_tokens': 4423, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfde9-78b1-7ff2-aac3-f491bdee9ea6-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_metrics', 'args': {'query': 'http_requests_total{job="hotel-reservation"}'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a1c1ae937d7c271a', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3933, 'output_tokens': 490, 'total_tokens': 4423}), ToolMessage(content='("{\'resultType\': \'vector\'